{"name":"Paternoster","hex":"#c7c7c6","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Paternoster","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative form of paternoster (“Lord's Prayer”).","A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Paternoster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paternoster, South Africa","blocks":[{"text":"Paternoster is one of the oldest fishing villages on the West Coast of South Africa. It is situated 15 km north-west of Vredenburg and 145 km north of Cape Town, at Cape Columbine between Saldanha Bay and St Helena Bay. The town covers an area of 194.8 hectares and has approximately 1880 inhabitants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Paternoster_South_Africa_1.jpg/330px-Paternoster_South_Africa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paternoster%2C_South_Africa"},{"title":"Paternoster (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Paternoster is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Angelo Paternoster (1919–2012), American football guard","Fernando Paternoster (1903–1967), Argentine footballer and manager","Henri Paternóster (1908–2007), Belgian fencer","Henry Paternoster (1882–1956), Australian rules footballer","Jim Paternoster (1875–1954), Australian rules footballer","Letizia Paternoster, Italian cyclist","Marissa Paternoster, American musician","Matt Paternoster (1880–1962), Australian rules footballer","Paola Paternoster (1935–2018), Italian retired athlete","Raymond Paternoster (1952–2017), American criminologist","Richard Paternoster (1802–1892), English civil servant","Roger Paternoster, Belgian field hockey player","Ron Paternoster (1916–2002), Australian rules footballer","Verusca Paternoster, Italian softball player","Vito Paternoster, Italian cellist"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paternoster_(surname)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/